Conclusion:
The cardiotocographic dataset was successfully analyzed using various exploratory data analysis techniques. Initial preprocessing included handling missing values using mean imputation to ensure data completeness and consistency. Descriptive statistics such as mean, median, standard deviation, and quartiles provided insights into the distribution and variability of the features. Visualizations including histograms, boxplots, and violin plots helped in understanding data distribution and identifying potential outliers. Outliers were explicitly treated using the IQR method by capping extreme values, which improved the robustness of the dataset without removing important observations. Correlation analysis using heatmaps and scatter plots revealed relationships between variables, while pairplots provided a comprehensive multivariate view of selected features. Overall, the dataset is well-cleaned, structured, and ready for further analysis or machine learning applications.